{"id":"CVE-2007-0726","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-03-13T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T12:26:54.411Z","description":"The SSH key generation process in OpenSSH in Apple Mac OS X 10.3.9 and 10.4 through 10.4.8 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service by connecting to the server before SSH has finished creating keys, which causes the keys to be regenerated and can break trust relationships that were based on the original keys.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.us-cert.gov/cas/techalerts/TA07-072A.html","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_CERT"],"name":"TA07-072A"},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/security-announce/2007/Mar/msg00002.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2007-03-13"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/22948","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"22948"},{"url":"http://docs.info.apple.com/article.html?artnum=305214","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1017756","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1017756"},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/34850","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"34850"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/32975","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"macos-openssh-dos(32975)"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2007/0930","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2007-0930"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/24479","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"24479"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2007-2243","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-04-25T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T13:33:27.475Z","description":"OpenSSH 4.6 and earlier, when ChallengeResponseAuthentication is enabled, allows remote attackers to determine the existence of user accounts by attempting to authenticate via S/KEY, which displays a different response if the user account exists, a similar issue to CVE-2001-1483.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://lists.grok.org.uk/pipermail/full-disclosure/2007-April/053906.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20070421 OpenSSH - System Account Enumeration if S/Key is used"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/23601","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"23601"},{"url":"http://securityreason.com/securityalert/2631","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SREASON"],"name":"2631"},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/34600","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"34600"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/33794","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"openssh-challenge-information-disclosure(33794)"},{"url":"http://lists.grok.org.uk/pipermail/full-disclosure/2007-April/053951.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20070424 OpenSSH - System Account Enumeration if S/Key is used"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20191107-0003/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2007-2768","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-05-21T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T13:49:57.388Z","description":"OpenSSH, when using OPIE (One-Time Passwords in Everything) for PAM, allows remote attackers to determine the existence of certain user accounts, which displays a different response if the user account exists and is configured to use one-time passwords (OTP), a similar issue to CVE-2007-2243.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/34601","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"34601"},{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/fulldisclosure/2007-04/0635.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20070424 Re: OpenSSH - System Account Enumeration if S/Key is used"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20191107-0002/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
